  {
    "episode_id": 74292,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74292.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Thank you, Congresswoman Clark. And I think you've just so much in that answer that we could dive into and we will. But I wanted to just press you on an aspect of it. You sort of situated us within this technological moment that we're in, in terms of artificial intelligence becoming this powerful technology that has the potential to perpetuate some of the injustices in our system. We're also having in this country, a real kind of racial reckoning, particularly over the last year, as the coronavirus pandemic has affected the country and we've had the killing of George Floyd and many other incidents, maybe you could just help us situate your interest in AI and AI bias in the context of this kind of bigger societal moment that we're in and really help us understand the implications of AI for race and for justice in this country.",
