  {
    "episode_id": 74292,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74292.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely, no question about that. You've described this before as a eureka moment when our inequities are revealed. And it's certainly, as you've explained through what's transpiring during the pandemic between having access to jobs. We've seen it in the New York Times recent article on algorithms deciding who has access to vaccines and leading to more complications through that black box algorithms. So there is a need, obviously, for regulation, for intervention to make sure that this is being handled in the most equitable way. Can you explain to us how the Algorithmic Accountability Act will help with this eureka moment? And can you explain for our listeners a little bit about how that helps answer some of the really issues of great concern that you've raised already on our conversation so far?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "There is a clear need for regulatory oversight and intervention to ensure equity in algorithmic decision-making.",
