        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "A recent New York Times article discusses how algorithms determine vaccine access and contribute to further complications.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Access to jobs during the pandemic has been unevenly distributed, contributing to visible inequities.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Algorithmic decision-making systems are inherently prone to bias unless actively regulated.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Transparency in algorithmic processes is essential for identifying and correcting inequities.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The public has a right to understand how life-altering decisions like vaccine allocation are made.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The Algorithmic Accountability Act is a credible and effective policy mechanism for addressing algorithmic injustice.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The listener values fairness and justice in technological systems, especially during crises like pandemics.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 74292,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74292.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "So what our bill does is it requires the FTC to require companies with data on over 1 million users or with revenue greater than 50 million to conduct bias and security assessments of highly sensitive automated decision systems and then fix any issues that they identify. What it does is that If companies don't audit their algorithms for bias, they can then act surprised when a researcher discovers that their software is perpetuating discrimination. The incentives are flipped with my bill. If you are undertaking due diligence to make sure that your systems are fair, you're not at risk of receiving a bad headline. You are liable under the law. And so what it does is it incentivizes the work that needs to be done to uproot and unearth any adverse and biased baked into the systems of most of the various platforms that we use. And I think it's critical because one of the things we know is that, you know, There are millions of users out there that just click the button because they want to use the app. They don't know exactly what is going on, but they want to use the app. Their information is immediately put into big data. And we know that at the end of the day, while AI systems, their conclusions are bought about based on calculations, that outputs can reflect bias of the programmers or the data sets that are ultimately used to train those systems. And so getting our companies to conduct this bias and security assessment is just the beginning of the work that needs to be done to unearth this. And we are hoping that as we move forward with this legislation, there will be some violence every work done in this space because right now, companies feel like they're profitable under their current methodology. And who wants to disrupt that? Well, we do because we want to make sure that this is an equitable society that we live in and that everything we do is mindful of bad practices that have discriminated against significant portions of our civil society.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Our bill requires the FTC to mandate bias and security assessments for companies with data on over 1 million users or revenue exceeding $50 million.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The bill applies specifically to highly sensitive automated decision systems.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Companies must fix any issues identified during these assessments.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "If companies fail to audit their algorithms for bias, they cannot claim surprise when researchers expose discriminatory outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "My bill flips the incentive structure so that proactive fairness efforts reduce legal liability rather than increase it.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Conducting bias and security assessments is foundational to identifying harmful biases embedded in platform systems.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Millions of users interact with apps without understanding how their data is processed.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "AI system outputs can reflect programmer or dataset biases despite being algorithmically generated.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Current corporate methodologies prioritize profit over ethical accountability.",
