    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Well, absolutely. This moment is not just a physical world moment. Again, there are so many individuals who are using our tech infrastructure right now from students who, you know, this could have long-term lifelong implications for to our seniors who, you know, whose health is at risk and where algorithmic bias in the healthcare space, you know, could mean, you know, adverse consequences for, you know, their longevity. There are so many ways in which we've got to use this moment to turn the page and to have our technology sector far more reflective of the lived experiences of the people that it serves. And it serves all of us. We're talking today via Zoom. And so it's critical that we use this moment to sort of crack the code on, no pun intended, on what could be a very protracted struggle to reverse engineer, if you will, biases that could be perpetuated for generations to come. And this administration has the infrastructure and the interests to get that done. And so I'm excited about it. And I think we will be able to move some really meaningful legislation as a result of that.",
